{% comment %}
  Home hero — Figma: Work Page → Hero (desktop 491:14843, mobile 458:6526).

  Two columns on desktop, stacked on mobile: a tinted panel carrying the copy
  beside the product shot, and a full-bleed marquee closing the section.

  The section owns the media, the panel and the marquee. Everything the merchant
  writes is a block: the headline, the sentence and each call to action stand in
  the panel's content area, and the review line is a static block pinned to its
  floor. See `docs/section-settings.md`.

  The panel spaces its blocks with one gap and lets a block that needs more air
  add it through the custom properties below, which the block only overrides when
  the merchant moves its own padding setting.

  The header is not built yet, so the section opens with a reserved band the
  height of the one the design draws. Turn `reserve_header_space` off the moment
  the real header lands, or the page gains a gap.

  The marquee runs on the theme's own `marquee-component`, which already handles
  cloning, speed and reduced motion — no new script, but it does need the theme's
  own one: marquee.js is not in the importmap, so the element upgrades only on a
  page that asks for the file. Without the tag below the component stays an inert
  HTMLElement and the words sit still.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign marquee_word = section.settings.marquee_text | default: 'krispie treat'
  assign marquee_repeat = section.settings.marquee_repeat | default: 8
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  The file sets the badge figure in Outfit Black. The theme carries the accent font
  at 500 with a bold variant, so 900 would otherwise be synthesised — the trap
  snippets/ui-kit-tokens.liquid documents for Nunito SemiBold. This loads the real
  face, and only on the pages that draw the badge. `font_modify` returns nothing
  when the family has no such weight, in which case the guard skips it and the
  browser falls back to synthesising, which is what would have happened anyway.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if section.settings.show_badge -%}
  {%- assign accent_black = settings.type_accent_font | font_modify: 'weight', '900' -%}
  {%- if accent_black -%}
    <style>{{ accent_black | font_face: font_display: 'swap' }}</style>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

<div class="section-background color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }}"></div>
<div
  class="home-hero color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }}"
  {% comment %}
    The height is written as two properties, one per breakpoint, rather than as
    --home-hero-media-height itself. An inline style outweighs any rule in the
    stylesheet, so setting the used property here would freeze one number across
    every width and the mobile step below could never reach it. The media query
    picks which of the two is used instead — the trap docs/section-settings.md
    documents.
  {% endcomment %}
  style="
    --home-hero-media-height-mobile: {{ section.settings.height_mobile }}px;
    --home-hero-media-height-desktop: {{ section.settings.height }}px;
    --home-hero-panel-justify: {{ section.settings.content_position }};
  "
  data-testid="home-hero-{{ section.id }}"
  {{ section.shopify_attributes }}
>
  <div class="home-hero__inner">
    <div class="home-hero__grid">
      <div class="home-hero__panel">
        <span class="home-hero__sparkle" aria-hidden="true">
          {{- 'icon-ui-sparkle.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
        </span>

        <div class="home-hero__body">
          {% content_for 'blocks' %}
        </div>

        {%- if section.settings.show_reviews -%}
          {% content_for 'block', type: '_ui-review-line', id: 'review-line' %}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      <div class="home-hero__media">
        {%- if section.settings.image != blank -%}
          {% render 'image', image: section.settings.image, height: 600, class: 'home-hero__image', loading: 'eager' %}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- comment -%} Photography is not in yet; hold the frame so the layout reads true. {%- endcomment -%}
          <span class="home-hero__image-placeholder" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.settings.show_badge and section.settings.badge_text != blank -%}
          <span class="home-hero__badge">
            {%- if section.settings.badge_figure != blank -%}
              <span class="home-hero__badge-figure">
                {{- section.settings.badge_figure -}}
                <span class="home-hero__badge-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                  {{- 'icon-ui-gluten-badge.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
                </span>
              </span>
            {%- endif -%}
            <span class="home-hero__badge-label">{{ section.settings.badge_text }}</span>
          </span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- if section.settings.show_marquee -%}
    <marquee-component
      class="home-hero__marquee"
      style="--marquee-direction: {{ section.settings.marquee_direction }};"
      data-speed-factor="25"
      data-movement-direction="{{ section.settings.marquee_direction }}"
    >
      <div class="marquee__wrapper" ref="wrapper">
        <div class="marquee__content" ref="content">
          <div class="marquee__repeated-items" ref="marqueeItems[]">
            {%- for i in (1..marquee_repeat) -%}
              <span class="home-hero__marquee-word">{{ marquee_word }}</span>
              <span class="home-hero__marquee-star" aria-hidden="true">
                {{- 'icon-ui-marquee-star.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
              </span>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </marquee-component>

    <script src="{{ 'marquee.js' | asset_url }}" type="module" fetchpriority="low"></script>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  /*
   * Home hero. Mobile first; the desktop layout starts at the theme's 750px
   * breakpoint.
   *
   * The gutter comes from --ui-page-margin so every section built from the file
   * steps at the same widths.
   */
  .home-hero {
    --home-hero-gap: 16px;
    /* Air between the header and the panel; the marquee sits outside it. */
    --home-hero-space-start: 20px;
    --home-hero-radius: 20px;
    --home-hero-panel-padding-block: 24px;
    /*
     * 14px, not the 24 the panel is padded above and below. The file stands a
     * 315 wide sentence and a 310 wide pair of buttons inside a 343 panel, and a
     * 24px inset leaves neither of them room.
     */
    --home-hero-panel-padding-inline: 14px;
    --home-hero-panel-gap: 32px;
    --home-hero-block-gap: 16px;
    --home-hero-sparkle-size: 24px;
    --home-hero-media-height: var(--home-hero-media-height-mobile, 416px);
    --home-hero-badge-inset: 16px;

    /* Marquee */
    --home-hero-marquee-padding: 20px;
    --home-hero-marquee-size: 16px;
    --home-hero-marquee-star: 14px;

    display: flow-root;
    background-color: var(--ui-color-white);
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .home-hero {
      --home-hero-gap: 20px;
      --home-hero-space-start: 32px;
      --home-hero-panel-padding-block: 32px;
      --home-hero-panel-padding-inline: 32px;
      --home-hero-panel-gap: 32px;
      --home-hero-sparkle-size: 32px;
      --home-hero-media-height: var(--home-hero-media-height-desktop, 600px);
      --home-hero-badge-inset: 20px;
      --home-hero-marquee-padding: 24px;
      --home-hero-marquee-size: 20px;
      --home-hero-marquee-star: 16px;
    }
  }

  .home-hero__inner {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    max-width: var(--page-width, 90rem);
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: var(--ui-page-margin);
    padding-block-start: var(--home-hero-space-start);
  }

  .home-hero__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--home-hero-gap);
  }

  /*
   * Between 750 and 990 the hero stacks, but at the width one of its columns is
   * drawn at rather than across the whole page. The panel is drawn 630 wide and
   * holds a 410 heading and a 356 pair of buttons; two columns at 750 give it
   * 325, where the heading falls to four lines and the buttons drop onto two
   * rows. A 900px band with a 400px column adrift in it is not the answer
   * either, so the stack keeps the column's own width and centres it.
   */
  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .home-hero__grid {
      max-width: 630px;
      margin-inline: auto;
    }
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 990px) {
    .home-hero__grid {
      /* The file splits 1280 into two 630 columns with 20 between them. */
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      max-width: none;
      margin-inline: 0;
    }
  }

  /* ---------- Panel ---------- */

  .home-hero__panel {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    gap: var(--home-hero-panel-gap);
    padding-block: var(--home-hero-panel-padding-block);
    padding-inline: var(--home-hero-panel-padding-inline);
    border-radius: var(--home-hero-radius);
    background-color: var(--ui-color-light-blue);
  }

  /*
   * The panel is as tall as the photograph beside it, which leaves it with far
   * more height than its contents need, and the merchant chooses where that
   * surplus goes.
   *
   * "Center" gathers the three parts into one group on the panel's own gap and
   * pushes the surplus out to the top and bottom edges, where it reads as air.
   * "Space between" is what the file draws — the sparkle on the ceiling, the
   * review line on the floor — and it wants the review line switched on to earn
   * it. Without one there are two children rather than three, nothing holds the
   * floor, and the whole surplus opens as a single hole under the sparkle. Hence
   * the default, and the note on the setting.
   *
   * Below 750px the panel has no min-height and hugs its content, so neither
   * arrangement has any surplus to place and the rule stays inside the query.
   */
  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .home-hero__panel {
      justify-content: var(--home-hero-panel-justify, center);
      min-height: var(--home-hero-media-height);
    }
  }

  .home-hero__sparkle {
    display: block;
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: var(--home-hero-sparkle-size);
    height: var(--home-hero-sparkle-size);
    color: var(--ui-color-primary);
  }

  .home-hero__sparkle > svg,
  .home-hero__badge-icon > svg,
  .home-hero__marquee-star > svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }

  /*
   * The content area. One gap holds the column together and the measurements the
   * file draws are handed to the blocks as custom properties: a block writes its
   * own only when the merchant moves the matching setting, so these are defaults
   * rather than overrides.
   *
   * The two link properties are added to the gap above, not used instead of it:
   * 16 + 16 puts the buttons 32 under the sentence on a phone, 16 + 32 puts them
   * 48 under it on a desktop.
   */
  .home-hero__body {
    --ui-heading-max-width: 275px;
    --ui-text-max-width: 315px;
    --ui-link-row-padding-start: 16px;
    --ui-link-padding-start: 0px;
    --ui-link-row-item-width: 100%;

    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--home-hero-block-gap);
    width: 100%;
    text-align: center;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .home-hero__body {
      --ui-heading-max-width: 410px;
      --ui-text-max-width: 416px;
      --ui-link-row-padding-start: 32px;
      --ui-link-padding-start: 8px;
      /* The kit sizes a button by its label; the file fixes both to one width. */
      --ui-link-row-item-width: 170px;
    }
  }

  /*
   * On a phone the buttons are a 310 wide stack. The row would otherwise shrink
   * to its content, and its children are asking for the row's own width.
   */
  .home-hero__body .ui-link-row {
    width: 310px;
    max-width: 100%;

    /*
     * Centred, which shows only once the row wraps. The file draws the three
     * buttons side by side at 1440, where the panel is the 630 it is drawn at;
     * between 990 and about 1390 the two columns leave the panel narrower than
     * the row's 542, so the third drops to a line of its own. It belongs under
     * the middle of the panel, with everything else in here, rather than
     * orphaned against its left edge.
     */
    justify-content: center;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .home-hero__body .ui-link-row {
      width: auto;
    }
  }

  /*
   * With the width fixed the labels have to stay on one line, which is what the
   * file sets, and the outlined button needs the tighter padding the kit gives
   * it or "Customize treats" will not fit inside 170px.
   */
  .home-hero__body .ui-link-row .ui-button {
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .home-hero__body .ui-link-row .ui-button--secondary {
    padding-inline: var(--ui-button-padding-inline-tight);
  }

  /*
   * The third call to action is a button beside the other two on a desktop and a
   * plain underlined link under them on a phone — the file draws both. One block
   * cannot carry two variants, so the phone is written here: the row's last item
   * drops the button's skin and takes [ui-button]'s underline look, which is a
   * transparent fill, no ring and a rule under the words.
   */
  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    /*
     * The row's last item, not the last button: every button is an only child of
     * its own [_ui-link] wrapper, so `.ui-button:last-child` is true of all three
     * and strips the skin off the whole stack.
     *
     * And only where there is a third to be tertiary. The same hero opens the
     * wholesale and corporate pages on a row of one — "Apply for wholesale",
     * "Send an inquiry" — and a lone primary button is the page's whole call to
     * action, not an afterthought under two others. `:nth-child(n+3)` is that
     * test: last, and at least the third.
     *
     * The wrapper is the flex item, so `align-self` on the button inside it
     * centres nothing — the row is already stretching the wrapper to its full
     * 310. Centring has to happen inside the wrapper.
     */
    .home-hero__body .ui-link-row > :nth-child(n + 3):last-child {
      justify-content: center;
    }

    .home-hero__body .ui-link-row > :nth-child(n + 3):last-child .ui-button {
      --ui-button-background: transparent;
      --ui-button-border-width: 0;

      align-self: center;
      width: auto;
      min-height: 0;
      padding: 0 2px 2px;
      border-block-end: 1px solid var(--ui-color-primary);
      border-radius: 0;
    }
  }

  /* ---------- Media ---------- */

  .home-hero__media {
    position: relative;
    border-radius: var(--home-hero-radius);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .home-hero__image,
  .home-hero__image-placeholder {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: var(--home-hero-media-height);
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .home-hero__image-placeholder {
    background-color: var(--ui-color-border-gray);
  }

  /*
   * The stamp on the photograph: a white plate with a purple frame set 3px inside
   * it, the figure over two lines with the wheat mark sitting in it, and the
   * wording beneath.
   */
  .home-hero__badge {
    position: absolute;
    inset-block-end: var(--home-hero-badge-inset);
    display: inline-flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 1px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 12px 20px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    background-color: var(--ui-color-white);
    color: var(--ui-color-primary);
    font-family: var(--ui-font-accent);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    white-space: nowrap;
    /* Centred on mobile, tucked into the corner on desktop. */
    inset-inline-start: 50%;
    translate: -50% 0;
  }

  /*
   * The frame is its own layer rather than the plate's own inset shadow: the file
   * sets it 3px in from the edge, which a shadow on the element itself cannot do.
   * Drawn above the text for the reason ui-quantity-stepper and ui-variant-select
   * both document — an inset shadow paints under its element's children.
   */
  .home-hero__badge::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 3px;
    border-radius: 5px;
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--ui-color-primary);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .home-hero__badge-figure {
    position: relative;
    font-size: var(--home-hero-badge-figure-size, 41px);
    /* Outfit Black. The face is loaded by this section rather than by the theme,
       which carries the accent font at 500 and its bold only. */
    font-weight: 900;
    line-height: 0.83;
  }

  /*
   * The mark sits in the figure rather than beside it, so it is placed by hand at
   * the offsets the file draws. Those are tuned to "100%" — a merchant who writes
   * something appreciably wider or narrower can move it with the two custom
   * properties rather than needing this rule changed.
   */
  .home-hero__badge-icon {
    position: absolute;
    inset-block-start: var(--home-hero-badge-icon-top, 6px);
    inset-inline-start: var(--home-hero-badge-icon-start, 24px);
    display: block;
    width: 13px;
    height: 23px;
  }

  .home-hero__badge-label {
    font-size: var(--home-hero-badge-label-size, 14px);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: var(--ui-line-height);
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .home-hero__badge {
      inset-inline-start: auto;
      inset-inline-end: var(--home-hero-badge-inset);
      translate: none;
    }
  }

  .home-hero__badge-icon {
    display: block;
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: 16px;
    height: 16px;
  }

  /* ---------- Marquee ---------- */

  .home-hero__marquee {
    --marquee-gap: 24px;

    margin-block-start: var(--home-hero-gap);
    padding-block: var(--home-hero-marquee-padding);
    background-color: var(--ui-color-primary);
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .home-hero__marquee {
      --marquee-gap: 32px;
    }
  }

  .home-hero__marquee-word {
    color: var(--ui-color-white);
    font-family: var(--ui-font-accent);
    font-size: var(--home-hero-marquee-size);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .home-hero__marquee-star {
    display: block;
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: var(--home-hero-marquee-star);
    height: var(--home-hero-marquee-star);
    color: var(--ui-color-sky-blue);
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Home hero",
  "tag": "section",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "_ui-heading"
    },
    {
      "type": "_ui-text"
    },
    {
      "type": "_ui-link"
    },
    {
      "type": "_ui-link-row"
    }
  ],
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "t:settings.color_scheme",
      "default": "scheme-1"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:content.media"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image",
      "label": "t:settings.image",
      "info": "Left empty, the frame is held with a placeholder."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_badge",
      "label": "Show the badge on the image",
      "info": "Off by default. Only switch it on with a claim the shop can stand behind.",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "badge_figure",
      "label": "Badge figure",
      "info": "The large line. The mark is placed for a short figure such as \"100%\"; a much wider or narrower figure needs it nudged.",
      "default": "Certified",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.show_badge }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "badge_text",
      "label": "Badge",
      "default": "gluten-free",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.show_badge }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:content.layout"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "height",
      "label": "t:settings.height",
      "info": "The photograph's height, and the least the panel beside it can be. The panel grows past it if the copy needs the room.",
      "min": 320,
      "max": 920,
      "step": 10,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 600
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "height_mobile",
      "label": "t:settings.mobile_height",
      "info": "Stacked, so this is the photograph alone — the panel above it is as tall as its copy.",
      "min": 240,
      "max": 640,
      "step": 8,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 416
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "content_position",
      "label": "t:settings.content_position",
      "info": "How the panel's spare height is used, on desktop. \"Space between\" pins the sparkle to the top and the review line to the bottom, so it needs the review line shown — without it the copy drops to the panel's floor.",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "center",
          "label": "t:options.center"
        },
        {
          "value": "space-between",
          "label": "t:options.space_between"
        }
      ],
      "default": "center"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Review line"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The faces, the stars and the rating are edited on the Review line block inside the section."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_reviews",
      "label": "Show the review line",
      "info": "Off by default. The manual rating and review count are unverified; switch on only with real figures.",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Marquee"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_marquee",
      "label": "Show the marquee",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "marquee_text",
      "label": "t:settings.text",
      "default": "krispie treat",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.show_marquee }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "marquee_repeat",
      "label": "Repeats",
      "info": "How many times the word is written before the strip is cloned to fill the screen.",
      "min": 4,
      "max": 16,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 8,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.show_marquee }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "marquee_direction",
      "label": "t:settings.direction",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "normal",
          "label": "t:options.left"
        },
        {
          "value": "reverse",
          "label": "t:options.right"
        }
      ],
      "default": "normal",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.show_marquee }}"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Home hero",
      "category": "t:categories.banners",
      "blocks": {
        "heading": {
          "type": "_ui-heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<h1>Who doesn't love <br><em>a Krispie Treat?</em></h1>"
          }
        },
        "copy": {
          "type": "_ui-text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>A modern take on the Krispie treat you grew up with. Handcrafted, certified gluten-free, and ready to give for birthdays, thank-yous, and just because.</p>"
          }
        },
        "buttons": {
          "type": "_ui-link-row",
          "blocks": {
            "primary": {
              "type": "_ui-link",
              "settings": {
                "label": "Shop treats",
                "variant": "primary"
              }
            },
            "secondary": {
              "type": "_ui-link",
              "settings": {
                "label": "Design your box",
                "variant": "secondary"
              }
            }
          },
          "block_order": [
            "primary",
            "secondary"
          ]
        },
        "gifting": {
          "type": "_ui-link",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Client and team gifts",
            "variant": "underline"
          }
        },
        "review-line": {
          "type": "_ui-review-line",
          "static": true,
